steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1785610675
      nanos: 788946712
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "You have the complete Llamacorp project. Diagnose and fix the current responsive-layout bug without changing the visual design, content, desktop layout, or component architecture unnecessarily.\n\nCurrent problem:\nOn mobile, the homepage hero is broken: the headline is cut off horizontally, content begins outside the viewport, there is an excessively large empty space below the navbar, the navbar has a blank area, and the CTA buttons extend edge-to-edge without proper page padding. See the attached screenshot.\n\nFirst inspect these files and any shared global styles they use:\n\n- `App.jsx`\n- `MagneticTopNavbar.jsx`\n- `SelectedWork.jsx`\n- `Services.jsx`\n- `Pricing.jsx`\n- `FAQ.jsx`\n- `CTA.jsx`\n- `CtaImageArc.jsx`\n- global CSS / Tailwind config\n\nFind the actual cause before changing code. Look specifically for mobile-inherited desktop styles: fixed/min widths, fixed heights, `translateX`, negative margins, absolute `left/right` offsets, oversized padding, `w-screen`, and transforms that cause overflow.\n\nImplement the following:\n\n1. Global safety\n- Prevent horizontal scrolling at all breakpoints.\n- Ensure page wrappers and sections use `width: 100%`, `max-width: 100%`, and `box-sizing: border-box`.\n- Do not use `100vw` inside padded parent containers if it creates overflow.\n- Preserve desktop visuals at 1024px and above.\n\n2. Hero at \342\211\244767px\n- Hero content must be centered and fully visible within 16px page padding.\n- Remove the large blank vertical space below the navbar.\n- Use a normal document-flow layout; do not use desktop absolute positioning or offsets on mobile.\n- Heading: fluid typography around `clamp(2.35rem, 10vw, 3.25rem)`, tight line-height, `max-width: 340px`, no clipping.\n- Paragraph: centered, max-width around 320px.\n- Buttons: stack vertically at 360px, remain pill-shaped, max-width 360px, minimum height 52px.\n- Keep testimonial pill and logo marquee, but make them fit without overflow.\n\n3. Navbar at \342\211\244767px\n- Compact floating navbar with logo, social icons if space permits, and \342\200\234Let\342\200\231s Work.\342\200\235\n- Hide desktop navigation links.\n- If 360px is too narrow, show logo + hamburger + \342\200\234Let\342\200\231s Work\342\200\235; put links/social icons inside the opened menu.\n- Navbar width must be `calc(100% - 32px)` with `max-width: 430px`, centered.\n\n4. Remaining responsive behavior\n- Portfolio: 1-column static/scrollable gallery on phone, 2 columns tablet, 4-column animated wall desktop.\n- Services, pricing, FAQ: one column on phone/tablet; retain desktop layouts only where space allows.\n- Final CTA: full available width without horizontal overflow; fewer arc cards on touch screens and no card covers text.\n\nVerification is required:\n- Run and inspect at 360px, 390px, 430px, 768px, 1024px, and 1440px.\n- Confirm no horizontal scrolling.\n- Before making unrelated changes, provide screenshots of the fixed hero at 360px and 430px and briefly list the exact root causes you fixed.\n- Work on a separate branch named `fix/mobile-responsive-layout` and do not deploy or modify production settings."
    items {
      text: "You have the complete Llamacorp project. Diagnose and fix the current responsive-layout bug without changing the visual design, content, desktop layout, or component architecture unnecessarily.\n\nCurrent problem:\nOn mobile, the homepage hero is broken: the headline is cut off horizontally, content begins outside the viewport, there is an excessively large empty space below the navbar, the navbar has a blank area, and the CTA buttons extend edge-to-edge without proper page padding. See the attached screenshot.\n\nFirst inspect these files and any shared global styles they use:\n\n- `App.jsx`\n- `MagneticTopNavbar.jsx`\n- `SelectedWork.jsx`\n- `Services.jsx`\n- `Pricing.jsx`\n- `FAQ.jsx`\n- `CTA.jsx`\n- `CtaImageArc.jsx`\n- global CSS / Tailwind config\n\nFind the actual cause before changing code. Look specifically for mobile-inherited desktop styles: fixed/min widths, fixed heights, `translateX`, negative margins, absolute `left/right` offsets, oversized padding, `w-screen`, and transforms that cause overflow.\n\nImplement the following:\n\n1. Global safety\n- Prevent horizontal scrolling at all breakpoints.\n- Ensure page wrappers and sections use `width: 100%`, `max-width: 100%`, and `box-sizing: border-box`.\n- Do not use `100vw` inside padded parent containers if it creates overflow.\n- Preserve desktop visuals at 1024px and above.\n\n2. Hero at \342\211\244767px\n- Hero content must be centered and fully visible within 16px page padding.\n- Remove the large blank vertical space below the navbar.\n- Use a normal document-flow layout; do not use desktop absolute positioning or offsets on mobile.\n- Heading: fluid typography around `clamp(2.35rem, 10vw, 3.25rem)`, tight line-height, `max-width: 340px`, no clipping.\n- Paragraph: centered, max-width around 320px.\n- Buttons: stack vertically at 360px, remain pill-shaped, max-width 360px, minimum height 52px.\n- Keep testimonial pill and logo marquee, but make them fit without overflow.\n\n3. Navbar at \342\211\244767px\n- Compact floating navbar with logo, social icons if space permits, and \342\200\234Let\342\200\231s Work.\342\200\235\n- Hide desktop navigation links.\n- If 360px is too narrow, show logo + hamburger + \342\200\234Let\342\200\231s Work\342\200\235; put links/social icons inside the opened menu.\n- Navbar width must be `calc(100% - 32px)` with `max-width: 430px`, centered.\n\n4. Remaining responsive behavior\n- Portfolio: 1-column static/scrollable gallery on phone, 2 columns tablet, 4-column animated wall desktop.\n- Services, pricing, FAQ: one column on phone/tablet; retain desktop layouts only where space allows.\n- Final CTA: full available width without horizontal overflow; fewer arc cards on touch screens and no card covers text.\n\nVerification is required:\n- Run and inspect at 360px, 390px, 430px, 768px, 1024px, and 1440px.\n- Confirm no horizontal scrolling.\n- Before making unrelated changes, provide screenshots of the fixed hero at 360px and 430px and briefly list the exact root causes you fixed.\n- Work on a separate branch named `fix/mobile-responsive-layout` and do not deploy or modify production settings."
    }
  }
}
