  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Mobile Layout Needs**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the mobile layout adjustments for the `SelectedWork` component, specifically for screens 767px and below. The primary goal is to achieve a two-column vertical layout. I\'m also double-checking the outer page padding; it seems like the existing `<section>` wrapper uses `px-4`, which I need to verify is the correct starting point for applying the required `12px` padding on mobile.\n\n\n**Refining Mobile Card Appearance**\n\nI\'ve determined the ideal padding should be `px-[12px]` and set a column gap of `8px`. Card widths will be `calc(50% - 4px)` to fit a 2-column layout. I\'ll stack cards vertically with an `8px` gap, subtle border, and light background. To create a seamless loop effect, I plan to duplicate cards and adjust their vertical offsets. The visual window will be around `720-900px` with `overflow-hidden`. Importantly, I will omit any horizontal scroll, and implement crisp images using `w-full h-auto object-cover`. I\'ve also reconsidered the existing overlay in `renderCard`, and am leaning towards retaining it as it\'s only visible on hover.\n\n\n**Adjusting Mobile Grid Structure**\n\nI\'ve decided to hide the overlay on mobile devices by using `hidden md:flex`, as per the design specifications. I\'m now restructuring the grid layout for mobile. Instead of a single column, I\'m aiming for two animated columns, using `col1` and `col2` data and removing the existing mobile static scrollable gallery. The new structure will be dynamic and scrollable.\n\n\n**Optimizing Grid Column Visibility**\n\nI\'m currently finalizing the mobile grid adjustments. I\'m ensuring that only the first two columns are visible on mobile, while the last two are reserved for desktop. I\'ve updated the grid to a responsive structure: two columns with an 8px gap on mobile, two columns with a 16px gap on tablet, and four columns with a 16px gap on desktop. The columns use dynamic animation classes; the new implementation uses different vertical offsets, applied via `animClass`, which is already working well.\n\n\n**Refining Vertical Offset Alignment**\n\nI\'m now focusing on achieving different starting vertical offsets for the columns to prevent synchronization, as per the specifications. I am considering several approaches, including using a negative top margin on the second column, as this will not be overridden by the animation\'s `translateY` property. Alternatively, adding padding to an outer container could also work. Further refinements include checking the requested card styling.\n\n\n**Revising Card Visual Styling**\n\nI am now updating the `renderCard` component based on mobile-specific design requirements. I\'ve adjusted the card styling. The updates address the card spacing, border, background, and image display with conditional class names. I\'ve implemented a `8px` gap, a subtle border, a light background, and have ensured that images are crisp and fully contained using `object-cover`. Furthermore, I\'ve hidden the overlay on mobile devices as specified.\n\n\n**Finalizing Card Component Style**\n\nI\'m now implementing the final refinements for the `renderCard` component\'s mobile styling. I\'ve focused on ensuring the visual presentation meets design requirements. I\'ve incorporated conditional class names for a rounded appearance on various screen sizes, background colors, borders, and a cursor effect. I\'m also addressing the image display for both video and image types, incorporating full width and object cover.\n\n\n**Refining Card Component Spacing**\n\nI\'m revisiting the spacing within the card components to eliminate redundancy. After analysis, the `mb-2 md:mb-4` on the `<a>` tag makes a `gap` on the container unnecessary, so I\'ll keep this on the card itself for consistency. I am still considering techniques to offset the grid columns; padding on the top of each column will allow different starting points for the card animations.\n\n\n**Revising Column Positioning**\n\nI\'ve determined that adding `pt-12 md:pt-24` to the animated container is ineffective for visual offsets. Instead, I\'ll apply it to the wrapper div. This will create the required vertical offset between columns, which is necessary for a staggered effect. I\'m focusing on the visual wall container.\n\n\n**Adjusting Container Visuals**\n\nI\'m now implementing the adjustments for the visual wall container. I\'m focusing on the responsive padding, border radius, and overall dimensions of the container. I\'ve considered that the page padding must be 12px, which translates to a `calc(50% - 4px)` card width. I\'m updating the `grid` to `grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4` with appropriate gaps. Further, I\'ve considered the card component adjustments for the visual style.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
