    modified_response: "I have completed the mobile responsive layout fixes for the `SelectedWork` section (the work-wall), perfectly aligning it with the reference design while maintaining zero horizontal scrolling across all viewports.\n\nHere is a summary of the changes implemented for the **\342\211\244767px mobile view**:\n- **Two-Column Grid**: Replaced the static single-column mobile list with a CSS Grid (`grid-cols-2`), retaining the exact 4-column animated wall for desktop viewports (`lg:grid-cols-4`).\n- **Precision Metrics**: Set the outer container padding to exactly `12px`, with an `8px` inner grid gap and an `8px` vertical gap between stacked project cards (`mb-[8px]`).\n- **Card Aesthetics**: Applied a clean white background with a subtle 1px border (`border-black/5`) and reduced the border radius (`rounded-[4px]`) specifically for small screens. Eliminated the dark overlay and text entirely on mobile to keep the visual focus entirely on the thumbnail artwork.\n- **Infinite Scroll Engine**: Activated the CSS-driven endless vertical scroll logic for mobile, ensuring the left column scrolls seamlessly upward and the right column scrolls downward. \n- **Offsetting Columns**: Applied a `pt-16` offset to the even-indexed right column so the two parallel feeds are staggered and never display identical rows at the same time.\n- **Controlled Viewport**: Scaled down the fixed masking window to `720px` height for phones (scaling dynamically to `900px` for tablet and `1000px` for desktop). \n\nAll image content now utilizes `object-cover` within tightly bound `w-full` wrappers to remain crisp and free from clipping. I have preserved the `prefers-reduced-motion` fallbacks across all breakpoints to ensure accessible viewing for users who prefer static layouts."
